1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,680
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,617
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,257
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:10,516
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,995
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,440
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,640
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,080
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,257
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,697
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:29,537
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:34,960
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:40,380
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:52,597
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:58,437
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,117
That legendary place.

18
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,817
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:06,717
Is only legendary?

20
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,137
Till someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:12,577
Through it all.

22
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,497
Through all the trouble and times.

23
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,837
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:19,577
Know that I will be there.

25
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,397
To stand by you.

26
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,220
Like I know you'll stand by me.

27
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:28,237
So come aboard and bring along.

28
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:30,560
All your hopes and dreams.

29
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:33,897
Together we will find everything.

30
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:36,040
That we're looking for.

31
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,737
There's always room for you.

32
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:42,480
If you wanna be my friend.

33
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,760
We are, we are on the crew.

34
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,720
We are.

35
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:22,968
That looks like it's ready.

36
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,920
Momoo! Lunchtime! Momoo!

37
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:32,700
Where is he?

38
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:34,180
Kinda weird.

39
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:37,260
I've never seen Momoo
show up late to a meal.

40
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,100
I wonder what happened.

41
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:48,310
Conis!

42
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:52,857
The possession of weapons is a
clear affront to my authority.

43
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:56,380
As an example to any other
would-be rebels in this town,

44
00:02:56,680 --> 00:03:01,100
I'm going to kill you right now so
they can see the fate that awaits them

45
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:02,960
No way,

46
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:09,020
that guy is insane He killed someone for
just having a weapon I won't land Hey,

47
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:10,050
wait,

48
00:03:10,133 --> 00:03:13,680
don't go out there You have
absolutely no right to do this, Arlong

49
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:18,397
We've paid your tribute
without fail for over

50
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:21,186
eight years Why would
we rebel against it now?

51
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:24,280
Just think about it It makes no sense!

52
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:27,600
Now take your hand off Genzo!

53
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:29,690
Yeah!

54
00:03:29,773 --> 00:03:33,660
It's not like he used the
weapons! That's right! Let him go!

55
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:35,460
Yeah, let Genzo go!

56
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:39,767
Hoarding weapons shows he was
planning a rebellion against me.

57
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:44,640
But, on the other hand,
I could destroy you all.

58
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:48,857
Please try to protect your friends so
you won't give me an excuse to do that.

59
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:53,060
Either way is fine, but
rebellions will not be tolerated.

60
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,740
Everybody just go home.

61
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:59,517
Do you want to waste all of our
work over the past eight years?

62
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:00,430
For what?

63
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:05,097
The time for you to give your lives for
this village was back when they first came.

64
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:07,500
Now we must continue to be patient.

65
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:10,917
The most important thing is
that we continue to live.

66
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,765
We swore we would not let them
defeat us as long as we're alive.

67
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:16,760
Gensang! No!

68
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:20,360
Well, Zed, I agree with you.

69
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:26,520
Here, it's good to know that even disgusting
insects like you enjoy being alive!

70
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:28,960
Oh, no.

71
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:35,025
There is no way any of you will ever come
close to the perfection of the Fistman!

72
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:38,220
Damn you! Don't move!

73
00:04:38,460 --> 00:04:40,500
He wants you to attack.

74
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,040
We can't just stand here!

75
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,620
Your deaths will mean nothing.

76
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:49,220
You must continue to be patient.

77
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:52,777
Even if I die!

78
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:54,497
That's a good ending for you.

79
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:57,197
Pay close attention, humans.

80
00:04:57,280 --> 00:05:00,257
This is what happens to those who defy me.

81
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:02,617
Even if it's inside their tiny heads!

82
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:03,860
Exploding stars.

83
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,420
What was that?

84
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:12,040
Up there, look.

85
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,800
There's someone on the roof!

86
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:18,500
Who the hell is that guy?

87
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:24,560
I am the great warrior of
the sea, Captain Usopp!

88
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:27,410
Usopp?

89
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:32,340
Also known as the Demon King Usopp,
feared and hated by almost half the world.

90
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:36,597
I command thousands of
men, loyal and vicious men.

91
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:40,974
That's the guy I told you about, the
one with the long nose and got away.

92
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,840
Bring on your thousands of men.

93
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:47,160
I'll crush them one by one.

94
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:51,739
The exploding star did
nothing, and now he's pissed.

95
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:53,840
Repulsive human.

96
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:57,180
What can a creature like you do to me?

97
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:06,742
Starlong, hold on just a second.

98
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:10,725
After losing Koza, we can't afford
to kill off any more tribute,

99
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:12,450
money!

100
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:16,257
Villages are fun to destroy, but
ruling over them makes us more money.

101
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,360
If we lose

102
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,597
some, we can always get more.

103
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:23,797
This man must reign to me!

104
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:25,480
He's destroying it all!

105
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:31,170
Usopp!

106
00:06:31,253 --> 00:06:32,940
Am I dead yet?

107
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:36,060
He's not dead yet! Oh crap! Get him!

108
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,360
Get him and tear him apart.

109
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:44,637
Let's go back to Arlong Quark
before he destroys everything!

110
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:46,420
Yeah, I'm with you.

111
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,017
Don't let him get away.

112
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:51,677
Who does that jumpsunker think he is?

113
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:52,600
We'll be back.

114
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:55,060
You can all live for now!

115
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,177
I'm so sorry, everybody.

116
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:04,937
This has all been my fault.

117
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,608
What are you talking about?

118
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:08,604
You're not a fish man, are you?

119
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:11,073
Yeah, but who was that guy who attacked?

120
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,080
Hello, everyone.

121
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,060
It's good to be back home.

122
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:17,630
Nami?

123
00:07:17,713 --> 00:07:18,740
It's Nami. You.

124
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:27,740
What's wrong?

125
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:31,037
You never just come walking
through Cocoyashi anymore.

126
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,740
I heard quite a commotion.

127
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,470
Arlong, huh?

128
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:47,920
I only have to get seven
million more berries.

129
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:52,400
Your already bad reputation
just keeps getting worse.

130
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:53,780
That's fine.

131
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,940
I am a pirate.

132
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:58,017
Arlong can be a very reasonable
guy when he wants to.

133
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:01,297
I just need a little more
money to finish our agreement.

134
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:04,615
Just seven million berries
shy of the 100 million gold.

135
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:08,877
You know it's really not that high a price

136
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:11,620
considering it's gonna
buy back our village.

137
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:18,157
She tells me to run but I've
got nowhere else to go but

138
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:22,837
here besides promised Luffy
I'd bring her back with me.

139
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:28,277
Man what's he up to because things
are getting messy around here?

140
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:32,640
That's mine I put it on my
plate that's how it works.

141
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,257
Sorry, how about you
eat this thing instead?

142
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:45,869
I wouldn't feed that
rotten slop to my dog.

143
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:49,720
Shh, quiet.

144
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,226
There's something down there.

145
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,020
It's big.

146
00:09:05,260 --> 00:09:06,780
What the hell is that?

147
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:10,720
Sea monster!

148
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,900
It's a cow.

149
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:18,360
Not cow.

150
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:19,561
They don't swim.

151
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,290
A hippo?

152
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:24,497
Whatever it is, you can tell
it's from the Grand Line.

153
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:27,815
What is it doing all the way
out here in the East Loop?

154
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:31,680
Why is he staring at us?

155
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:38,300
He wants the food! What?

156
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:41,980
Clint, give it to him before
he sinks the ship! Gum-Gum!

157
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:50,800
Bad sea cow, stay away from our food! Ha!

158
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,920
Yes, you knocked it out!

159
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,760
Oh crap, you made it mad!

160
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,220
It's back for more!

161
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:03,217
Dumbass, there's no reason to
punch this poor, hungry hippo.

162
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:09,237
she's probably just a baby and can't
catch food for herself yet huh that right?

163
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,897
you're insane.

164
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:13,197
here you go, eat up.

165
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:14,597
don't be scared.

166
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:15,621
i won't hit you.

167
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:28,037
what the hell are you doing?

168
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,897
damn jerk.

169
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:32,317
it was gonna eat me with the plate.

170
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,420
what could i do?

171
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:40,937
stand back.

172
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:42,260
this is my show.

173
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,720
Oh, yeah, cool!

174
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:53,420
That's that.

175
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:58,870
Yes!

176
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,160
Back to the food!

177
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:01,820
That was refreshing.

178
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:04,540
You guys are insane. Seriously.

179
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:09,440
What's taking so long?

180
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,280
Luffy, where are you?

181
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:19,011
Five more minutes of this, and
I'll keel over from boredom.

182
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:22,550
Incredible!

183
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:23,597
What are you?

184
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,100
Some kind of super fish?

185
00:11:25,340 --> 00:11:26,980
Not even the mighty Hachan!

186
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:30,477
Octopusnator of the Arlong Pirates
can pull you from the ocean!

187
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:31,780
What an epic battle!

188
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:36,335
I don't know who you are, but you're
the gutsiest fish in the East Blue!

189
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:38,377
Hey, what the...?

190
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,320
It was me all along?

191
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:47,457
You are indeed the gutsiest
fish in the East Blue, me!

192
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,580
Hold on, that's weird!

193
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:51,480
It sure is?

194
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:53,620
Hey, who are you?

195
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,720
Speak up now

196
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:57,860
Who? Me?

197
00:11:58,060 --> 00:12:02,860
Well, I'm Hatchan, but all my friends
call me Hatchi Are you a fish man too?

198
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:06,797
Of course, of course, I'm
an amazing octopus fish man.

199
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:09,177
It looks to me like you're just a human.

200
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:11,320
Uh, yeah. A marine!

201
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:12,880
Or possibly a guest!

202
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,440
A guest?

203
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,960
Uh, you could say that.

204
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,820
Arlong isn't here, is he? No.

205
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:23,077
I thought you might know where he is.

206
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:26,857
Apparently, there's some long-nosed
guy running around causing trouble.

207
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:29,705
So Arlong locked up the
long-nosed friend here,

208
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:33,577
then went to Cocoyashi Village to
hunt down that pesky troublemaker.

209
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:34,820
Oh, man. Who's up?

210
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,942
Well, I guess I better save him.

211
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,960
It's Cocoyashi Village.

212
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,980
How do I get there? Get in!

213
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:50,700
You're a guest. Hop in.
I'll take you. Swordsman.

214
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:05,120
Oh, man.

215
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:06,811
I can't shake these guys.

216
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:12,500
Hey, where'd he go?

217
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:16,980
All those in favor of
leaving Usopp alone say aye!

218
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:20,400
Aye! Aye! Aye! Aye!

219
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:23,440
You fool, you're dumber than I thought.

220
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:26,620
Ah, you agree with me too! That's great!

221
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,200
Eggstar, special attack!

222
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,900
Oh, I think I'm gonna roll!

223
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:50,537
I guess fishmen aren't all
they're cracked up to be!

224
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:52,857
Not one of those scaly morons
can catch Captain Usopp!

225
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:53,770
Hehehe!

226
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:11,180
Huh? Hey! Huh? What?

227
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:14,870
Ah!

228
00:14:14,953 --> 00:14:16,780
Yeah, I'm fine! Thanks for asking!

229
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:19,806
I made it down safe and
sound, as you can see!

230
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:26,079
Cocoyashi Village.

231
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:28,917
Orlong should be around here somewhere.

232
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,617
Oh, great, thanks!

233
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:32,560
No problem, bye now.

234
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,757
Oh, one more thing!

235
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:39,252
I completely forgot to ask you your name?

236
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:40,500
What do you mean?

237
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:43,052
We've been over this, I told you my name.

238
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:45,420
Hachan Nice to meet ya.

239
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:48,680
That was strange.

240
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:03,757
What the hell happened here?

241
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:07,380
Who did this to you?

242
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:20,160
What do you say?

243
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:22,130
Rolanoa.

244
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,140
Saru. What?

245
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:25,920
Pirate hunter?

246
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:28,200
Has he come to collect my head?

247
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,340
We had him.

248
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:35,180
That man we got, that was him.

249
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:39,100
He was Saru. That's him? Yes.

250
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:42,060
The swordsman was Rolanoa.

251
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:46,530
Two.

252
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:49,260
Ah Long, found him.

253
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,900
What is this?

254
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:55,500
Don't tell me that Zoro's...

255
00:15:58,580 --> 00:16:01,760
Catching this scum isn't
enough to satisfy my hunger.

256
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:06,450
Oh yeah?

257
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:08,360
Well, then let me go.

258
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:10,157
Oh, and I'm sorry about earlier.

259
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,497
I was just saying hello.

260
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:13,580
That's how we do it in my village.

261
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:18,320
Longnose, you are one of Zoro's men

262
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:24,180
It's only natural for well-known
bounty hunters to come after me

263
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:31,440
Please don't kill me I don't have
